        "id": 6628,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-06T17:59:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I posted a couple of pix to my randomizer site last night, and looking over the list of all heroes in the game, I noticed a trend.&nbsp; If you look at the hp of the original heroes, you'll see plenty of 30s and many high-20s. Rook City heroes were still relatively robust as well.&nbsp; Argent Adept seems to be the first victim to whatever is slowly killing the heroes though, because his hp is a low 24, and the trend worsens the closer we get to the shattered future:</p><p>Omnitron-X: 25 hp. Dark Visionary: 25 hp.&nbsp; Freedom Tempest, Price of Freedom Wraith, Golem Unity, all 25 hp.&nbsp; If the trend continues, Chrono-Ranger will barely be able to stand!</p><p>In all seriousness, I'm assuming that the hp have been dropping as the base powers have been getting better, which isn't a bad thing.&nbsp; Or maybe over time, the game designers have decided that the starting heroes had too many hp?&nbsp; I wonder if we'll ever see any true 30+hp tanks anymore.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:38.923Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
